            <ArticleTitle>A review of knee pain in adolescent females.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-36; quiz 36-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000466496.11555.ec</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary care practitioners are in a position to educate patients and parents about the risk factors that may increase the incidence of knee pain in adolescent females. This article highlights patellofemoral pain syndrome, Sinding-Larsen-Johansson syndrome, Osgood-Schlatter disease, and meniscal tears.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
